module tasks.`2026-11-20-den-readable-counterexamples-statechart`

task DenReadableCounterexamplesStatechart {
  title "Take from handoff formal-talk 0f06597b6: Den counterexamples in the spec's words, and the statechart view / den_statechart tool"
  verify $ cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-den -p bboxy450-code && make test-formal
  paths "crates/bboxy450-den", "crates/bboxy450-code", "scripts/test-formal.py", "verification/README.md", "ATTRIBUTION.md"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; minimize concepts; report what you removed.

    ## Source
    `origin/handoff/formal-talk-20261120` commit `0f06597b6` (2026-11-17, base `e513642b0`). It cherry-picks cleanly onto `origin/main` `f17cc5295` (Oracle checked; nothing of it is on main).

    ## Take
    - `crates/bboxy450-den` checker/render/lib/tests: X601 counterexamples name the claim's own sentence and each step's event, case and changed fields; X651 loops the same; the repair hint no longer suggests weakening the property. The old one-line trace format goes (replaced, not kept beside).
    - `bboxy450_den::statechart` (Mermaid reachable graph, false-invariant states marked, up to 16 states in a lowered spec's Views) and `bboxy450-code` `den_statechart` with its query tests.
    - The matching `scripts/test-formal.py` lines, and only the `verification/README.md` lines describing the two items above.
    - Keep the commit's "Inspired by" credit (Lauren Tan, pstack, no code copied) in the commit message and ATTRIBUTION.md if the repository records inspirations there.

    ## Drop (Oracle ruling)
    - `crates/bbt-mux/src/adapters/skills/bboxy450/SKILL.md` step 3: it adds ~15 lines to every seat's launch prompt and repeats the mandate that `AGENTS.md`/`verification/README.md` already hold (say it once).
    - `scripts/formal-drift.py` and the `make formal-drift` target: advisory, and `make land` already selects checks from the diff.

    ## Steps
    Worktree: the Oracle names it when a build slot is free. `git cherry-pick -n 0f06597b6`, restore the dropped paths, one signed commit, the verify, `make land` (one gate machine-wide), report.
    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-20 19:50: worktree
    - Worktree `/Users/feral/mydev/bbx-den`, branch `exec/den-statechart`, from origin/main `b0dbefa4c`. Start with `python_execute_orient` and do the cherry-pick, restore and checks from one `python_execute` program.
    - Write each long command's output and exit code under `target/den-handoff/` (`<step>.log`, `<step>.exit`) so the Oracle can resume from evidence if your session ends. One gate machine-wide.

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-20 19:58: credit beside the code, not ATTRIBUTION.md
    - Do **not** edit `ATTRIBUTION.md` or its 38 crate mirrors (no `make sync-licenses` for this task).
    - Put the credit where the policy wants it, beside the distinctive implementation: a compact comment at the `statechart` module/function in `crates/bboxy450-den` ("Inspired by Lauren Tan, \"All Code Is Slop (Except Mine)\", pstack statechart skill, https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack; ideas only, no code copied. Policy: https://github.com/bboxy450/bboxy450-term/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md"), and the same line in the commit message. `make test-licenses` stays green unchanged.

    ## Operator ruling, 2026-11-20 20:45: no external inspiration credit (supersedes the two credit instructions above)
    Operator: "we were doing TLA+ and LEAN before that talk, we are doing our own thing!"
    - Do **not** add any "Inspired by" credit, comment or commit-message line for Lauren Tan, the talk or pstack. Remove it if already written; the source commit `0f06597b6`'s message text about it is not carried over.
    - Our own formal work (TLA+/TLC, Yarn, Den, Lean) predates it; credit nothing external for this change. No ATTRIBUTION.md edit.

    ## Operator ruling, 2026-11-20 20:50: FINAL credit wording (supersedes every credit instruction above)
    Operator chose: credit the talk as inspiration.
    - Exactly one short line, in the commit message and as a comment beside the `statechart` code in `crates/bboxy450-den`: `Inspired by Lauren Tan's talk "All Code Is Slop (Except Mine)".`
    - Nothing more: no pstack link, no "ideas only/no code copied" phrasing, no claim about where our TLA+/Lean work came from, no ATTRIBUTION.md edit.

    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-20 22:10: licence baseline fixed on main
    - `e3253bb96` on origin/main gives `crates/bbt-mux/tests/fixtures/inbox_harness.py` the standard owned-source notice (`make test-licenses` exit 0). Rebase onto origin/main and continue; do not edit the fixture.


    ## Report from seat:01M7Y5ACT1TFKXQ1KPXG3ZENQ7

    [[Done]] Landed Den’s claim-level X601 and X651 traces and Mermaid statecharts on `origin/main` in signed commit `adff0bd14eabe88fab05d2025c2fae10e79295e4`. The focused suites passed 74 tests, the Views boundary drew 16 states and counted 17, and the landing gate passed with a 970-model formal receipt. The landed license check passed. Replaced event-only traces and the weakening hint, and dropped the handoff’s prompt step and formal-drift tooling.

